course: dictionary
lesson: 208
title: Words about health
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alcoholism is a noun for an illness. A person with alcoholism cannot stop drinking alcohol, even when it harms them and the people around them. «Alcoholism, or alcohol addiction, is an illness in which a person needs alcohol so badly they cannot stop even when it hurts them and their family.»
explain: Look at the clues in that sentence. Illness tells you it is a health problem, not a choice made once. The words needs and cannot stop show that it is very hard to control. Just as with famished, the words around a new word tell you what it means.
explain: Stories often use the words suffer from alcoholism and treatment for alcoholism. Suffer shows someone is going through something painful. Treatment means the help they get, from doctors and groups. «People can get better with help.»
fact: Alcoholism is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you cannot say "an alcoholism" or "two alcoholisms."
fact: «Alcoholism» means an illness in which a person cannot stop drinking alcohol, even though it harms them.
fact: «Alcohol addiction» is another way to say alcoholism.
fact: In Ireland, «the drink» can mean alcoholism: «He had a problem with the drink.»
fact: People with alcoholism can get better with help from doctors and support groups.
exercise: «Alcoholism is an illness in which a person needs alcohol so badly they cannot stop.» What is alcoholism? | A choice made once and then forgotten | *An illness where a person cannot stop drinking alcohol | A kind of drink sold in shops | A type of sport
exercise: In Ireland, someone says «He had a problem with the drink.» What does the phrase mean? | Forgetting where he put his keys | Liking a cup of tea too much | *Alcoholism, being unable to stop drinking alcohol | Being thirsty after a run
exercise: Which word in «a person needs alcohol so badly they cannot stop» shows that it is hard to control? | *Needs | Illness | Alcohol | Family
test: What does «treatment» mean in «treatment for alcoholism»? | A type of drink | A holiday | A bill from a shop | *The help a person gets to get better
test: Which best describes alcoholism? | A happy habit that everyone shares | A type of food | A problem with a bike | *An illness that harms the person and their family
exam: The sentence «Alcoholism, or alcohol addiction, is an illness» tells you that alcohol addiction means the same as | Shopping | Sleepiness | Being cold | *Alcoholism
